russia says some of its troops involved  in military drills near ukraine are  pulling back and returning to their  bases after completing the exercises the  drills have been a significant factor in  the crisis between russia and ukraine  which along with western nations fear  moscow is planning an invasion  on monday the kremlin suggested  diplomacy is still possible in diffusing  the standoff  let's go straight to dorset jabari's  live for us in moscow so tell us a bit  more about  these russian forces that are returning  to their bases  is it significant  well it certainly is and we've just been  hearing from the chief spokesperson of  the russian defense ministry major  general igor konoshenkov who has issued  a statement saying that some of russia's  western and southern military units will  be on their way back to their home bases  upon completing a series of military  maneuvers the major general also went on  to say that there are other further  units that are finishing up their  military drills and will be  going back to their home bases this is  of course something we heard from the  russian defense minister on monday  sergey shougo at a meeting with the  russian president vladimir putin said  that this was about to take place that  the military drills that were ongoing  for the past few weeks were coming to an  end and most of the military units that  have been dispatched alongside the  country's borders will be returning to  their home bases of course this will be  seen as the first significant step in  the current situation that we're in and  possibly seen as a sign of russia really  de-escalating the situation and sticking  to the word saying that these uh troop  movements were all to carry out these  drills and now that they're rebasing  them they really are going back to where  they were in the beginning and  reiterating this country's position that  they never really intended to invade  ukraine this was just a hysteria  narrative that was built by the western  countries  well perhaps the days and days of  diplomacy  is leading to something we have more  diplomacy today with the german  chancellor arriving in russia or already  in russia we're not 100 sure yet  what are we expecting from meetings  between schultz and putin today  well the german chancellor will be  talking about three main things with the  russian president first trying to  de-escalate the current crisis with  ukraine  and second on the agenda we'll be  talking about uh the security guarantees  that russia is looking for when it comes  to nato's further expansion and then the  third will be talking about that very  important uh north stream two gas  pipeline that was an 11 billion project  that took russian gas from siberia  transferred to  germany via the sea and not bypassing  any specific country this is a project  that was completed in september but has  yet to become operational due to certain  restrictions placed on it by the german  government many here accuse  germany of turning this pipeline into a  geopolitical tool the german chancellor  will certainly be discussing this with  the russian president and of course this  is not the only meeting that is taking  place here today the russian foreign  minister sergey lavrov will also  is currently meeting with his polish  counterpart the polish foreign minister  is in moscow to hold meetings about the  current situation and the  osce's concerns when it comes to the  current crisis that is ongoing so there  is still very much a diplomatic path  that is being pursued by many sides and  this latest announcement by the russian  defense ministry will certainly be an  important one given uh the day that  we're having in moscow the diplomatic  push to try and de-escalate the tensions  okay thank you for that daughter jabari  there for us live in moscow we can turn  now to step vassen who's live in pinsk  which is in western belarus where russia  has been holding some of the drills uh  steph i wonder what you can see where  you are especially in light of the fact  that russia says some of the troops that  have been involved in military drills  are now being pulled back  yes i'm mean pins that's uh 30  kilometers from the ukrainian border and  this uh historical town has quite a a  big population from uh ukrainians so  there's a lot of concern here also at  this border about its russian military  exercises happening so nearby the  belarusian authorities have released  some locations where these joint drills  are still ongoing but since uh yesterday  i have to say we've been traveling  around this region the southern border  of belarus with ukraine and it was very  quiet there was supposed to be exercises  air defense  fighter jets in actions even  bombardments at a place not very far  from here but so far it's very difficult  to see that there's a very large-scale  military exercise ongoing meanwhile of  course we know that  russia is now saying that they have  finished these exercises or are  finishing up these exercises and are  withdrawing troops we haven't seen any  signs of that but it could mean that  definitely these exercises are closing  and there's not much activity here but  people are telling us here they're not  very optimistic that russian forces will  leave that soon and they're quite  worried that the russians are actually  using this military exercise as a  pretext to basically occupy belarus and  have permanent bases here and that's  something that a lot of belarusians are  definitely not agreeing with  okay many thanks for that step vassen  monitoring the situation from pinsk in  western belarus
 

